    "text": "Best restaurants in Berlin according to an American #expat #lifeabroad #berlin #foodies ",
    "subtitles": "Here's the three best restaurants in Berlin that remind me a lot of the U. S.\nNo. 1 is fine bagels. Best bagel in Berlin.\nI don't give a fuck what you say,\nit's still the best one. And they have the best chocolate chip cookie.\nNo.2 is Manello.\nThat is a pizza place in vetting that although it's run by Italians,\nthey have stuffed crust pizza you cannot get to anywhere else.\nI don't even think Pizza Hut sells that shit anymore.\nSo if you're if you wanna get like that digorno style 90s Pizza Hut shit,\nyou gotta go there. I swear to God it is so fucking good.\nIt's actual stuffed crust pizza.\nLegit decent and fucking good.\nAlso not too bad, like 15 bucks give or take. Whatever.\nNumber three best restaurant if you really wanna fulfill that kind of like\nAmerican Oof that you've been lacking a bit.\nIt's actually gonna be like a two two combo.\nRebel Room in Berlin. It's like a burger place.\nTheir burgers are like legit,\nlegit, actually good.\nAnd No. 2 is actually Burger Am,\nbut not for their burgers.\nTheir French fries are legit on fire.\nI gotta say, I really love it.\nSo what I'm curious about is what do you think about my list?\nLet me know in the comments.\nAmericans, what are the like,\nrestaurants that you like?\nThe. The kind of restaurants in Berlin that are really good,\nthey remind you a little bit of Home.\nAnd for the Germans out there.\nWhat are the restaurants that you think that I'm missing?\nThat you think that are very American?\nLet me go ahead and rate that shit,\ncause I promise I'm ruthless.\nI cut them off, you know what I mean?\nBut I'm also an open minded person as well, so.\nBy the way, awesome.\nJonathan American has been in Berlin for over 10 years.\nEvery day I'm posting videos.\nIf you wanna give me a follow,\nshare this video, like it,\nwhatever, I'd be very grateful.\nPeace out and stay tuned for more fucking thing,\nyou know what I'm saying? Bye.",
